,{"words":[{"surface":"படுபு","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"set/sink"},{"text":"பு","lemma":"pu","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having set"},{"surface":"அறியலனே","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"aṟi","gloss":"know"},{"text":"அலன்","lemma":"alaṉ","gloss":"he does not"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"he does not know indeed"},{"surface":"பல்கதிர்","parts":[{"text":"பல்","lemma":"pal","gloss":"many"},{"text":"கதிர்","lemma":"katir","gloss":"ray"}],"gloss":"many-rayed"},{"surface":"செல்வன்","parts":[{"text":"செல்வன்","lemma":"celvaṉ","gloss":"lord/sun"}],"gloss":"lord (the sun)"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யானோ","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"yāṉ","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"interrogative/emphasis"}],"gloss":"as for me"},{"surface":"தஞ்சம்","parts":[{"text":"தஞ்சம்","lemma":"tañcam","gloss":"easy/insignificant"}],"gloss":"insignificant"},{"surface":"பெரும","parts":[{"text":"பெரும","lemma":"பெரும","gloss":"O great lord!"}],"gloss":"O great lord!","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இவ்","parts":[{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"this"},{"text":"வ்","lemma":"v","gloss":"demonstrative consonant"}],"gloss":"this"},{"surface":"உலகத்து","parts":[{"text":"உலகத்து","lemma":"உலகத்து","gloss":"of the world"}],"gloss":"of the world","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சான்றோர்","parts":[{"text":"சான்றோர்","lemma":"cāṉṟōr","gloss":"noble/virtuous people"}],"gloss":"noble people"},{"surface":"செய்த","parts":[{"text":"செய்த","lemma":"செய்த","gloss":"that did"}],"gloss":"that did","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நன்றுண்டாயின்","parts":[{"text":"நன்று","lemma":"naṉṟu","gloss":"good deed/virtue"},{"text":"உண்டு","lemma":"uṇṭu","gloss":"exists"},{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if there is good deed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இமையத்து","parts":[{"text":"இமையத்து","lemma":"இமையத்து","gloss":"of the Himalayas"}],"gloss":"of the Himalayas","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஈண்டி","parts":[{"text":"ஈண்டு","lemma":"īṇṭu","gloss":"gather/assemble"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having gathered"},{"surface":"இன்குரல்","parts":[{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"sweet"},{"text":"குரல்","lemma":"kural","gloss":"sound/thunder"}],"gloss":"sweet sound"},{"surface":"பயிற்றி","parts":[{"text":"பயிற்று","lemma":"payiṟṟu","gloss":"make repeatedly/practice"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having made repeatedly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கொண்டல்","parts":[{"text":"கொண்டல்","lemma":"koṇṭal","gloss":"east wind/cloud"}],"gloss":"east wind cloud"},{"surface":"மாமழை","parts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"mā","gloss":"great"},{"text":"மழை","lemma":"maḻai","gloss":"rain"}],"gloss":"great rain"},{"surface":"பொழிந்த","parts":[{"text":"பொழி","lemma":"poḻi","gloss":"pour"},{"text":"ந்த்","lemma":"nt","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"that poured"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நுண்பல்","parts":[{"text":"நுண்","lemma":"nuṇ","gloss":"fine/tiny"},{"text":"பல்","lemma":"pal","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many fine"},{"surface":"துளியினும்","parts":[{"text":"துளி","lemma":"tuḷi","gloss":"drop"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"than"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even/also"}],"gloss":"even more than the drops"},{"surface":"வாழிய","parts":[{"text":"வாழ்","lemma":"vāḻ","gloss":"live"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"optative suffix"}],"gloss":"may you live"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"pala","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"many indeed"}]}],"literal":"Even for those who cut the cow's udder, devoid of virtue, / and those who destroy the foetus of women wearing excellent ornaments, / and those of evil deeds who transgressed against their elders, / there exist ways of expiation, they say. / Even if the earth shifts from its place, / for those who destroy a benefit done, there is no escape, / so has righteousness declared, O husband of the well-adorned one! / Morning and evening, / mixing the cooked millet, which looks like the egg of a pigeon, with milk and honey, / and with kinsfolk who shredded the rich roasted meat of a small hare, / in the wide common ground where jujube trees grow tall, / with a heart free of concealment, uttering desired words, / to the bards who ate to satisfaction the thick heap of rich cooked rice, / he who bestowed never-leaving wealth completely, / 'May our king Valavan live long!' saying, if I do not sing of your / great and strong feet, / the sun of many rays does not know setting! / As for me, I am insignificant, O great lord! If there is any good deed / done by the noble people of this world, / may you live many more years than the many fine drops / of the great rain poured by the clouds of the east wind, / gathering over the Himalayas and making sweet sounds repeatedly!","translation":"Even for those who cut the cow's udder, devoid of virtue, and those who destroy the foetus of women wearing excellent ornaments, and those of evil deeds who transgressed against their elders, there exist ways of expiation, they say. Even if the earth shifts from its place, for those who destroy a benefit done, there is no escape, so has righteousness declared, O husband of the well-adorned one! Morning and evening, mixing the cooked millet, which looks like the egg of a pigeon, with milk and honey, and with kinsfolk who shredded the rich roasted meat of a small hare, in the wide common ground where jujube trees grow tall, with a heart free of concealment, uttering desired words, to the bards who ate to satisfaction the thick heap of rich cooked rice, he who bestowed never-leaving wealth completely, 'May our king Valavan live long!' saying, if I do not sing of your great and strong feet, the sun of many rays does not know setting! As for me, I am insignificant, O great lord! If there is any good deed done by the noble people of this world, may you live many more years than the many fine drops of the great rain poured by the clouds of the east wind, gathering over the Himalayas and making sweet sounds repeatedly!","modern":"பசுவின் மடியை அறுத்த அறமற்றவர்களுக்கும், சிறந்த அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த பெண்களின் கருவை அழித்தவர்களுக்கும், தம் அறிவுரை கூறும் பெரியோர்களுக்குத் தீங்கு செய்த கொடியவர்களுக்கும் கூடப் பாவ விமோசனம் உண்டு என்று கூறுவர். இந்த நிலமே நிலைபெயர்ந்து போனாலும், ஒருவன் செய்த உதவியை மறந்தவர்க்கு (நன்றி கொன்றவர்க்கு) உய்வு இல்லை என்று அறநூல் பாடுகின்றது, சிறந்த அணிகலன்களை அணிந்தவளின் கணவனே! காலையிலும் மாலையிலும், புறாவின் முட்டையைப் போன்ற புன்புல வரகரிசிச் சோற்றைப் பாலும் தேனும் கலந்து பிசைந்து, சிறிய முயலின் கொழுத்த இறைச்சியைப் பகிர்ந்துண்ணும் சுற்றத்தாரோடு, இலந்தை மரங்கள் நிறைந்த அகன்ற மன்றத்தில், ஒளிவு மறைவற்ற நெஞ்சத்தோடு இன்சொல் பேசி, குவியலான சோற்றை வயிறார உண்ட பாணர்களுக்கு நீங்காத செல்வத்தை முழுமையாக வழங்கியவன், 'எம் அரசன் வளவன் வாழ்க!' என்று வாழ்த்தி உனது பெருமை பொருந்திய வலிமையான பாதங்களைப் பாடாமல் போனால், பல கதிர்களை உடைய ஞாயிறு மேற்றிசையில் மறையவே மாட்டான்! பெருமானே! இவ்வுலகத்துச் சான்றோர் செய்த நல்வினை என்று ஒன்று இருக்குமாயின், இமயமலையில் திரண்டு இனிய இடிக்குரல் எழுப்பிக் கொண்டல் மேகம் பொழிந்த நுட்பமான பல மழைத்துளிகளைக் காட்டிலும் பல ஆண்டுகள் நீ வாழ்வாயாக!","explanation":"The poet Alathur Kizhar is praising the Chola king Kulamuttrathu Thunjia Killi Valavan. He emphasizes the gravity of ingratitude by comparing it to the worst sins like killing a cow, causing abortion, or harming elders, for which expiations exist, whereas there is no redemption for ingratitude. The poet describes the king's immense generosity towards bards, who are fed with rich food like millet mixed with milk and honey, and roasted hare meat, in the common assembly ground. He declares that if he does not sing the praise of such a generous king, the sun itself would refuse to set. Finally, he blesses the king to live for more years than the raindrops that fall from the clouds over the Himalayas, invoking the merit of all the good deeds done by noble people in the world.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,1.7],[1.7,3.1],[3.1,3.2],[3.2,4.23],[4.3,4.5],[4.5,5.7],[5.7,6.1],[6.1,6.3],[6.3,6.5],[6.5,7.9],[7.9,8.0],[8.0,8.92],[8.92,9.1],[9.1,9.3],[9.3,10.4],[10.4,10.7],[10.8,11.3],[11.3,11.5],[11.5,12.6],[12.6,13.2],[13.2,13.37],[13.59,13.7],[13.7,14.0],[14.0,14.5],[14.5,14.82],[14.9,15.4],[15.4,15.9],[15.9,16.8],[16.8,17.2],[17.2,17.5],[17.5,17.9],[19.08,19.71],[19.71,20.13],[20.18,20.68],[20.68,20.78],[20.78,21.38],[21.58,22.08],[22.08,22.18],[22.18,22.58],[22.58,23.88],[23.88,24.19],[24.35,24.98],[25.13,25.2],[25.78,26.28],[26.28,26.28],[26.28,26.28],[26.28,28.03],[28.03,28.78],[28.78,29.28],[29.28,29.78],[29.78,30.28],[30.28,31.18],[31.18,31.58],[31.58,31.88],[31.88,32.28],[32.28,33.58],[33.58,33.98],[33.98,34.38],[34.38,34.48],[34.48,35.38],[35.38,35.78],[35.78,35.98],[35.98,36.48],[36.48,36.68],[37.4,38.0],[38.0,38.2],[38.2,38.9],[38.9,39.0],[39.0,40.12],[40.12,40.2],[40.2,40.75],[40.75,41.4],[41.4,42.3],[42.3,42.5],[42.5,43.08],[43.2,43.39],[43.39,43.9],[43.9,44.8],[44.8,45.1],[45.1,45.4],[45.47,45.8],[45.8,47.0],[47.0,47.0],[47.0,47.6],[47.6,47.9],[47.9,49.0],[49.0,49.2],[49.2,49.6],[49.6,50.7],[50.7,51.3],[51.3,51.8],[51.8,52.0]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,1.7],[1.7,3.2],[3.2,3.3],[3.3,4.33],[4.4,4.6],[4.6,5.7],[5.7,6.1],[6.1,6.3],[6.3,6.5],[6.5,7.9],[7.9,8.0],[8.0,8.78],[8.78,9.0],[9.0,9.3],[9.3,10.4],[10.4,10.7],[10.7,11.3],[11.3,11.7],[11.7,12.7],[12.7,13.2],[13.2,13.46],[13.72,13.9],[13.9,14.2],[14.2,14.9],[14.9,15.14],[15.2,15.9],[15.9,16.4],[16.4,17.3],[17.3,17.6],[17.6,17.9],[17.9,18.2],[19.44,20.12],[20.12,20.54],[20.54,21.04],[21.04,21.14],[21.14,22.04],[22.34,22.84],[22.84,22.94],[22.94,23.44],[23.44,24.84],[24.84,25.21],[25.4,26.14],[26.29,26.36],[26.44,26.44],[26.44,26.44],[26.44,26.44],[26.44,27.96],[27.96,30.24],[30.24,30.62],[30.62,30.81],[30.99,31.64],[31.64,32.74],[32.74,33.24],[33.24,33.44],[33.44,33.94],[33.94,35.54],